BRXSRCHD                                                         MAINTC command

Use the BRXSRCH command to setup a minidisk search order to build and
modify a CMS "debug" version of the bREXX interpretor. The debug version
contains tracing and extra runtime messages for debugging.

The format of the BRXSRCHD command is:
+----------+------------------------------------------------------------------+
| BRXSRCHD |                                                                  |
+----------+------------------------------------------------------------------+

Usage Notes:

1. The minidisk search order after issuing this command is:

   MNT191  191  A    R/W     Work disk where compiled code is created
   MNT293  293  E/A  R/O     TEXT files for the compiled debug bREXX code
   MNT193  193  F/A  R/O     TEXT files for the compiled bREXX code
   MNT393  393  G/A  R/O     bREXX source code
   MNT394  394  H/A  R/O     GCC H files for CMS specific runtime
   MNT194  194  I/A  R/O     GCCLIB MACLIB for compiled bREXX code
